all of these puppies.

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:58.691 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Here's what happened.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:03.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
One looks just like Spartacus,
like his clone,

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.265 line:92%
and one looks just like Maximus.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:09.068 line:92%
So we named Max's son Tita

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the other one's name
is Little Spart.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.439 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And Chanel is happy.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.041 line:92%
And now we have four dogs.

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:16.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
The trick is, you got to -
I mean,

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:17.677 line:92%
when I get in bed at night

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.112 line:92%
it's like lion country safar

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:22.582
because I've got Chanel
who still sleeps with us.

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:23.449 size:75% position:38% line:92%
She climbs into bed.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:24.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's got her own room
and everything,

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:26.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
but she prefers
Mommy and Daddy's bed.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then we've got -- you know
you have kids, they want to --

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.592
you know, you're like, "Look
at how beautiful your room is.

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:34.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like, "Right,
I'll put my toys there."

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:36.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-"I'm coming up with you guys.

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:39.031 size:84% position:42%
And then I got the dogs
running around the bed.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's --
it's an interesting situation.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have, of course,
many projects,

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.442 line:92%
other shows outside of "SVU.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:51.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a new show
called "The Mediator,"

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:53.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you actually mediate
disputes.

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:55.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
What have you learned
from this show that's differen

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:57.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
from everything else
you've done up to this point

00:06:57.984 --> 00:07:01.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what it is, Seth
I started a production company

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
called Final Level
Entertainment.

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:04.524 line:92%
And we started putting shows -

00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:06.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm learning
from my mentor Dick Wolf

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
that one show
is not good enough.

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:12.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I have a show called
"In Ice Cold Blood" on Oxygen,

00:07:12.799 --> 00:07:15.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
one called "Framed by the
Killer" on Oxygen

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:16.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then this one came up,
"The Mediator."

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
So my guys that work on my tea
were like,

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:21.741 line:92%
"Conflict resolution, Ice,

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:22.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're the best person
for that."

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "I'm not no judge,
dude.

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:26.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not wearing no robe.
I'm not --"

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:29.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said, "No, mediation.
Mediation."

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:30.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they caught my ear
and they said,

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:33.453
"Now you have to go to mediation
before you go to court."

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:36.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I realized
that every human being

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:39.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
has mediated something
at some point.

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:39.892 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You've done it.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:41.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
You get between your brother
and your sister.

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.563 line:92%
You get between your friends

00:07:43.563 --> 00:07:47.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
Someone wants a neutral person
to get in between it.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.634 line:92%
So the beauty of the show

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:51.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
is I'm trying to help people
solve problems.

00:07:51.838 --> 00:07:54.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's nothing
like court because --

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
well we also have
a lawyer there,

00:07:56.042 --> 00:07:57.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
so once they tell me
the problems,

